find the perimeter of this hexagon so  the perimeter just means the distance  around the object or if you add up all  of the lengths of the sides of the  object so we're going to add up all the  lengths of sides of this hexagon and  hexagon is just a six-sided geometrical  shape like this so to find the perimeter  we just need to find the distance around  the hexagon which is going to be the sum  of all of the lengths of the sides so  the perimeter is going to be 24 so how  many of these do we have we have one two  three four five six  24s which makes sense because the  hexagon has six sides so we're gonna  have 24 let me write this a little bit  bigger 24 plus we write it like this  plus 24 plus 24 plus 24 plus 24 and  let's see that's five 24 so we're going  24 so let's add them all at the same  time we could have done it piece by  piece but let's just go straight ahead  so let's go first at the ones place so 4  plus 4 4 plus 4 is 8  8 plus 4 is 12 12 plus 4 is 16 16 plus 4  is 20 20 plus 4 is 20 4 is 24 and now  we're in the tens place 2 plus 2 is 4  plus 2 is 6 plus 2 is 8 plus 2 is 10  plus 2 is 12 plus 2 is 14 plus 2 is 14  so the sum of these six 24s is 144 that  is the perimeter and when we learn  multiplication if you haven't learned it  already you could have done this simpler  you say you have 6 24 so this would  actually be a multiplication problem of  6 times 24 if you don't know how to do  that just yet don't worry about it you  can just add them all up you get 144
 

